# The first Decision vertex: records the adoption of the Decision base type
# itself (0.3.0 base protocol). Doubles as the worked example of the shape —
# chosen / rejected / revisit-when in bounded prose. No template, no status
# field; written once at the moment of collapse.
"@context": "urn:bedrock:context/v1"
"@id": "urn:bedrock:vertex/decision-adopt-decision-records"
"@type": "urn:bedrock:ontology/Decision"
label: "Decisions are first-class records"
statement: >
  Chose to represent architecture decisions as Decision vertices in record/,
  with a supersedes edge forming the append-only chain floor invariant 15
  legislates. Rejected: markdown ADR directories (a second truth outside the
  graph — strands edges, forces full-document reads, the antithesis of
  progressive disclosure); a stored status field (liveness is derivable from
  the supersession chain; stored status would drift from it); separate
  decision/decision-record vertex pairs (the record is the decision's only
  durable form — two vertices double ceremony for zero assurance). Revisit if
  decision volume makes the record/ graph noisy to walk, or if consumers need
  register-level visibility of live decisions.
timestamp: "2026-08-23T11:09:05"
requires: "urn:bedrock:vertex/invariant-15-decisions-append-only"
references:
  - "urn:bedrock:vertex/invariant-01-possibility-space"
